{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "description": "Authoritative Cursor model catalog: the verbatim result of Cursor.models.list(), wrapped with provenance and the documented spec grammar. This registry is the only place Pancreator records what models and parameters Cursor accepts.",
  "source": {
    "method": "Cursor SDK Cursor.models.list()",
    "retrieved_by": "operator",
    "retrieved_at": "2026-08-17",
    "documentation": [
      "https://cursor.com/docs/subagents#model-configuration",
      "https://cursor.com/docs/sdk/typescript#model-parameters",
      "https://cursor.com/docs/sdk/typescript#cursormodelslist"
    ],
    "refresh": "Re-run Cursor.models.list() (or `cursor-agent --list-models` for a quick id check) and replace the models array with the verbatim result — both the verbatim and the compact encoding are valid registry content, and the loader expands either. To restore the compact form, pass the array through compressCursorModels in src/lib/executors/cursor-catalog-codec.ts, which verifies its own losslessness by round-trip. Agents MUST NOT hand-edit, infer, or partially update the models array, and MUST NOT record Cursor model facts anywhere else."
  },
  "grammar": {
    "spec_form": "<model-id>[<param>=<value>,...]",
    "notes": [
      "Bracket notation is Cursor's documented grammar for the subagent `model:` field and the CLI --model flag: 'Append square brackets to a model ID to set per-model options... Write options as id=value pairs, and separate multiple options with commas.'",
      "Parameters are PER-MODEL. GPT-family models take `reasoning`; Claude, Grok, and Gemini families take `effort`; Claude models also take `thinking` and `context`. Valid values also differ per model (gpt-5.5 uses `extra-high` where gpt-5.6-sol uses `xhigh`). Never carry a parameter or value from one model to another.",
      "A bracketed spec MUST specify every declared parameter of the model; a bare id (no brackets) is valid and delegates the variant choice to Cursor. Observed 2026-08-17 on the cursor-agent CLI: claude-fable-5[] and claude-opus-5[context=300k,effort=high] are rejected with 'Cannot use this model', fully-specified forms resolve to exactly the requested variant, and bare gpt-5.4 resolves to a Cursor-chosen default ('GPT-5.4 272K High' — note this differs from the models.list isDefault variant, so bare ids trade determinism for brevity.)",
      "Failure modes differ by surface: the cursor-agent CLI rejects an unusable spec loudly ('Cannot use this model' plus its slug inventory), while the IDE agent-frontmatter surface was observed on 2026-08-17 to degrade silently to a default variant when handed an invalid parameter name (effort= on gpt-5.6-sol ran at Medium). Pancreator validates before projection so neither surface is reached with an invalid spec.",
      "Runtime verification: probe with `cursor-agent -p --output-format stream-json --model \"<spec>\"` and read the resolved model from the system/init event (e.g. 'GPT-5.6 Sol 272K High').",
      "History: v3.5.0 rejected `reasoning=`/`thinking=` and rewrote specs to a flat `<model>-<effort>` slug; a v3.7.0 draft emitted `effort=` for GPT models. All were invalid against this list and degraded runs to default variants. Validate against the models array; do not invent grammar."
    ]
  },
